Observability: SDD

Purpose:
  The .sdd system's observability, runtime diagnostics and incident
   engine component. This directory defines how production runtime will
   be monitored, log/metrics/trace policy, alerting rules, health check
   mechanism, and incident lifecycle. Project-specific runtime state is
   stored in .sdd/instances/vkard.az/observability/. Separation: root = reusable
   observability constraints, project = concrete runtime state.

Owns: ./

ReadOrder:
   1  @logging.sdd
   2  @metrics.sdd
   3  @tracing.sdd
   4  @ai-observability.sdd (AI execution observability)
   5  @alerting.sdd
   6  @health.sdd
   7  @diagnostics.sdd
   8  @incident.sdd

Modes:
  MONITOR   — runtime monitoring and health check
  ALERT     — alerting and incident detection
  DIAGNOSE  — root cause analysis and diagnostics
  INCIDENT  — incident lifecycle management
  RECOVER   — recovery and rollback decision support

Rules:
  [OBS1]  Observability data MUST be treated as evidence, not assumption.
  [OBS2]  AI MUST correlate metrics, logs, and traces before diagnosing.
  [OBS3]  Alert severity MUST be project-contextual (payment failure
          = CRITICAL, internal admin latency = WARNING).
  [OBS4]  Incident MUST be distinguished from alert: alert = suspicion,
          incident = confirmed business/system impact.
  [OBS5]  Root cause analysis MUST include confidence level, not just
          likely cause.
  [OBS6]  Incident ? Task flow MUST be automatic for confirmed incidents.
  [OBS7]  Recurring failures MUST trigger ARCHITECTURE_REVIEW_REQUIRED.
  [OBS8]  Deploy correlation MUST be maintained: incident ? suspected
          deploy ? code change.
  [OBS9]  Sensitive data (password, token, session, card, secret, PII)
          MUST NOT appear in logs; violation = SECURITY_VIOLATION.
  [OBS10] Rollback decisions for production MUST respect project policy
          (AUTO or HUMAN_APPROVAL).

Entry:
  Read:
    INDEX.sdd

  Resolve:
    logging
    metrics
    tracing
    alerting
    health
    diagnostics
    incident

Navigation:
  Observability: @observability/INDEX.sdd
  Logging: @observability/logging.sdd
  Metrics: @observability/metrics.sdd
  Tracing: @observability/tracing.sdd
  AIObservability: @observability/ai-observability.sdd
  Alerting: @observability/alerting.sdd
  Health: @observability/health.sdd
  Diagnostics: @observability/diagnostics.sdd
  Incident: @observability/incident.sdd
  ProjectObservability: @instances/vkard.az/observability/INDEX.sdd

State: +
  Note:
  Observability directory created as
  the production runtime monitoring and incident response layer.
  Root observability/ defines reusable observability knowledge
  (logs, metrics, traces, alerting, health, diagnostics, incident);
  instances/vkard.az/observability/ tracks concrete project runtime state
  (services, alerts, incidents, diagnostics). This phase completes
  the development ? runtime ? feedback loop.
